  "briefing": "## Situation\nDaylight, haze. Post Alpha sits in a mountain valley. FPV drones guided over a fibre-optic cable have been reported in this sector: they emit no radio signal and cannot be jammed.\n## Mission\nDetect, identify and defeat the FPV before it reaches Post Alpha. Leave birds and friendlies alone.\n## ROE\nWEAPONS TIGHT — intercept only tracks you have classified as a threat type and declared HOSTILE. No intercepts inside the marked no-kinetic zones (settlements).\n## Assets\n- Radar, EO/IR camera and RF detector on high ground near the asset\n- RF jammer, 2.0 km, ±10° sector, 10 s cycle\n- GNSS spoofer, 2.0 km, ±10° sector, 15 s cycle\n- Interceptor, 1.5 km, 2 rounds, 6 s reload\n## Intel\nExpect a low approach along the valley from the south-east, hidden by the ridges until late. The RF detector will hear nothing from it, and the jammer will not stop it: the interceptor is the answer.",
